<title>PORTUGAL: YIELD RISES ON PORTUGAL 3-YR BONDS.</title>
<headline>YIELD RISES ON PORTUGAL 3-YR BONDS.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the result of the Portuguese Institute for Public Credit Management auction of 25 billion escudos of three-year fixed-rate bonds (OT).</p>
<p>ISSUER: Republic of Portugal</p>
<p>MATURITY:23/3/2000</p>
<p>AMOUNT PLACED: 25 billion escudos     COUPON:5.375</p>
<p>AVERAGE ACCEPTED YIELD: 5.3492</p>
<p>HIGHEST ACCEPTED: 5.35  LOWEST: 5.34</p>
<p>BIDS: 61.25 billion escudos PAYMENT FREQUENCY:Annual</p>
<p>PAYMENT DATE: 20/8/97</p>
<p>@</p>
<p>NOTES: The issue is fungible. The auction takes to 249.63 billion escudos the total amount of the bonds issued.</p>
</text>
